{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Boggman","id":"860303482065256448","is_bot":0,"username":"boggman1"},"author_id":"860303482065256448","channel_id":"850779383656218636","content":"Volt Thrower Firearm (chaingun) Ammunition (range 50/150), burst fire only, heavy, two-handed Very Rare: 10, 000 By this point the General had been raised up to having control over most of the surrounding lands. He approached the artificer with a gleam of arrogance and commanded he be made a weapon that the Gods themselves would kneel to and truly show his dominion over all. As always the Artificer went right to work, a gleam in his eye. A large platinum multi barreled gun attached to a hefty ammo pack, slung over shoulders with thick metal chains, was the result of his work. The barrels crackle with electricity as the gun spins up. While attuned to this you have resistance to lightning damage. Spin Up Before you make a burst attack with the chaingun, it must spin up. This takes a bonus action. Once the chaingun is spinning, it remains spinning until the end of your next turn in which you do not attack with it. Lightning Shackles Bolts of lightning spray from the barrels as you pull the trigger on the spun up gun. You choose up to 5 targets that are all within at least 15 feet of one of the other targets. They must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, they take 4d8 Lightning damage and are restrained as the electric current surges through their body’s, or half as much and suffer no other ill effects on a success. Static Burst As a reaction to getting hit by an attack and as long as the chaingun is spun up, you can make all creatures within 5ft of you make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw. Taking 2d8 lightning damage and disadvantage on the next attack they make on a failure or half as much and no disadvantage on a success. After using this you need to Spin Up again.(edited)","created_at":"2021-07-20T13:39:02.113000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867037891476717578","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
